16. Final acceptance criteria

The audit is complete only when:

1. The actual application and relevant Firebase configuration have been inspected.
2. All material findings are documented.
3. Safe fixes have been implemented.
4. Regression tests have been run.
5. Existing business rules and working features remain intact.
6. Critical authorization and financial operations use trusted controls.
7. Firebase Security Rules and relevant indexes have been tested.
8. City Partner and Admin onboarding remain isolated.
9. Buyer and Store Owner registration still work.
10. The deployment pipeline has been validated without unauthorized production deployment.
11. Remaining external configuration and verification tasks are explicitly documented.
12. The final report distinguishes proven results from assumptions.

Do not declare the application production-ready while any unresolved P0 or P1 finding remains. If critical live Firebase settings cannot be verified, state that full production readiness remains unverified.

START EXECUTION

Begin with repository discovery, actual Firebase configuration inspection, and baseline testing.

Proceed through the complete audit and safely implement every authorized fix available in the current environment. Do not stop after generating a checklist or audit plan.

Preserve the existing project and data. Stop before any action that could alter production data, cause financial transactions, change billing, expose credentials, weaken security, or deploy to production without explicit approval.

At the end, provide the complete findings register, implemented fixes, actual test results, unresolved blockers, and an evidence-based release recommendation.